# Live BJLA (Background Job Liveness Authority) records — STUB
#
# This ACT does not exercise the LIVE qualification step (no VS Code
# instance in this actuator environment). The LIVE step is deferred to
# a future ACT.
#
# When LIVE is qualified, this file will be the post-run dump of the
# "Cline Debug: Dump Background Job Liveness Authority" command, showing
# the bound set of:
#
#   job_cancellation_requested (with requestOrigin and firstWriterWins)
#   job_status_lookup
#   job_active_inserted
#   job_active_removed
#
# The decisive negative evidence (the GREEN invariant) is the ABSENCE
# of any job_cancellation_requested with requestOrigin=caller_abort_signal
# for the detached job after the caller aborts.
#
# The decisive positive-control evidence is the PRESENCE of exactly one
# job_cancellation_requested with requestOrigin=background_cancel_rpc when
# the operator clicks the explicit Cancel button on the Backgrounded card.
